conventions, OS-waitable completion tokens that IO/GPU fences plug into. | req ['C-BASE'] \nC-TASK 1 job-system-task-graph | Task graph & job API | Task creation, dependencies, priorities/QoS, blocking rules, completion-token integration, process-wide thread inventory with pinned/affinity lanes and middleware adapters, serial deterministic test mode and schedule-per | req ['C-SYNC', 'C-MEM'] \nC-INSTR 1 observability-telemetry | Instrumentation | Log/trace/metric API; zero cost when compiled out; trace format. | req ['C-BASE'] \nC-CRASH 1 crash-diagnostics | Crash & diagnostic hooks | Crash context annotations, breadcrumbs, watchdog registration. | req ['C-BASE', 'C-INSTR'] \nC-DET 1 determinism-replay | Determinism | Determinism levels, floating-point rules, ordered-execution rules, state-hash hooks. | req ['C-MATH'] \nC-BUDGET P performance-architect | Budgets & performance gates | Budget numbers per hardware tier × configuration × refresh class, derived from the performance model; perf gate thresholds. | req [] \nC-PLUGIN 1 plugin-system | Plugin descriptor & loading | Plugin manifest, dependency resolution, load phases, ABI tags. | req ['C-MOD'] \nC-FRAME 2 frame-orchestration | Frame, tick phases & time | Time domains and multi-rate cadences, pipelining depth, the minimal set of named global sync points, frame-wide access declarations (ECS components and registered service resources) from which ordering is derived, the ca | req ['C-TASK'] \nC-ID 2 entity-object-model | Identity & references | Entity IDs, GUIDs, reference kinds, lifetime rules, events. | req ['C-TYPES'] \nC-ECS 2 ecs-runtime | ECS | Components, queries, systems, access declarations, command buffers. | req ['C-ID', 'C-TASK', 'C-FRAME'] \nC-REFL 2 reflection-metadata | Reflection & type metadata | Type registry, properties, attributes, dynamic invocation. | req ['C-TYPES'] \nC-SER 2 serialization-schema | Serialization & schema evolution | Formats, versioning, upgraders, canonical form, untrusted-input rules. | req ['C-REFL'] \nC-IO 2 async-io-storage | Async IO | IO requests, priorities, deadlines, completions, decompression targets. | req ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK'] \nC-VFS 2 package-formats-vfs | Package & VFS mounts | Package format, mount layering (base, patch, DLC, mods, remote), chunk IDs, integrity; codec per target constrained by available hardware decompressors. | req ['C-IO', 'C-SER'] \nC-ASSET 2 content-pipeline-architect | Asset identity & references | Asset IDs, soft/hard references, dependency declaration, registry queries. | req ['C-SER', 'C-ID'] \nC-RES 2 resource-streaming-architect | Resource lifetime & streaming requests | Resource handles and explicit lifetime; load requests with priority/deadline; the staged load pipeline (IO → decompress → fixup → GPU upload → publish) that every resource type implements; pool registration, pressure sig | req ['C-ASSET', 'C-VFS', 'C-MEM'] \nC-RELOAD 2 hot-reload-iteration | Hot reload | Change notifications, invalidation, state preservation hooks. | req ['C-RES', 'C-MOD'] \nC-SPATIAL 2 spatial-transforms | Transforms & spatial queries | Transform representation incl. large-world coordinates, hierarchy, generic spatial queries, per-phase change sets (moved/attached/teleported) consumed by all spatial replicas. | req ['C-MATH', 'C-ID'] \nC-RHI 2 rhi-core | Render hardware interface | Devices, queues and command recording, completion tokens, binding-model tier (bindless / descriptor-buffer / bind-group), pipeline-state-model tier (monolithic PSO / libraries / shader objects / state-object programs), G | req ['C-PAL', 'C-MEM', 'C-SYNC'] impl\nC-GPUMEM 2 gpu-memory-resources | GPU resources & memory | Resource creation, heaps, residency, upload/readback, lifetime. | req ['C-RHI'] \nC-ML 2 ml-inference-runtime | ML inference | Model format and packaging, CPU and NPU backends, async invocation, precision classes, budgets. | req ['C-TASK', 'C-MEM'] \nC-WORLD 3 world-architect | World partition & streaming cells | Cells, streaming sources, world data activation in budgeted, time-sliced batches with bulk registration. | req ['C-SPATIAL', 'C-RES'] \nC-RG 3 render-graph-scheduling | Render graph | Pass/resource declaration, queues, history resources, readback, dynamic GPU-generated work nodes; barrier output mapped or elided on implicit-sync backends. | req ['C-RHI', 'C-GPUMEM'] \nC-SHADER 3 shader-system | Shader interface & interop | Shader modules, permutations and budgets, binding layouts generated per binding tier, interop headers, neural/tensor intrinsics tier. | req ['C-RHI'] \nC-MATIF 3 material-system | Material interface | Material parameters, shading model inputs, material domains. | req ['C-SHADER'] \nC-RSCENE 3 render-architect | Render scene & render features | Render features and views, render-scene data streams extracted as change-tracked deltas (no per-object proxy mirror; CPU cost O(changes)), feature registration with minimum GPU tier, non-mesh primitive kinds. | req ['C-RG', 'C-SPATIAL', 'C-MATIF'] \nC-TEMPORAL 3 reconstruction-upscaling | Temporal data | Motion vectors, jitter, history validity, reactive/transparency masks, resolution scaling; motion-vector obligations for every moving/animated surface; UI/HUD separation for frame generation; depth+motion submission for  | req ['C-RG'] \nC-RT 3 ray-tracing-infrastructure | Ray queries | Ray-query contract with hardware and software (SDF/BVH compute) backends: acceleration structures, instance data, hit/material binding, update policy. | req ['C-RSCENE'] \nC-TEXT 3 text-fonts | Text layout & glyphs | Shaped glyph runs, font fallback, glyph atlas/curve data. | req ['C-TYPES'] \nC-DRAW2D 3 render-2d-vector | 2D draw lists | Batched 2D/vector/text draw submission used by UI, 2D games, debug overlays. | req ['C-RG', 'C-SHADER', 'C-TEXT'] \nC-PHYS 3 physics-architect | Physics world & scene queries | Bodies, shapes, queries (handle-addressed, batched), contact events with budgets, stepping phases, batch add/remove O(batch), snapshot/restore/resimulate participation, collider history for rewind. | req ['C-SPATIAL', 'C-FRAME', 'C-ID'] \nC-ANIM 3 animation-architect | Animation pose output | Pose output and control input (parameters, action/montage requests, instance lifetime), root motion, animation events, pose history for rewind, network-sync hooks, physics/render hand-off. | req ['C-SPATIAL', 'C-ID'] \nC-AUDIO 3 audio-architect | Audio emitters & events | Emitter/listener data (multiple listeners), event triggering, parameters, busses, the sample-accurate audio clock exposed to gameplay. | req ['C-SPATIAL', 'C-ID'] \nC-INPUT 3 input-system | Input actions | Action definitions and values, tick-stamped input-command frames and their serialization (all targets incl. server); device binding contexts are client-side. | req ['C-FRAME'] \nC-NET 3 network-architect | Netcode model & authority policy | Netcode model per game type, authority model, net tick and time policy, compatibility window and handshake policy. | req ['C-FRAME', 'C-ID'] \nC-SVC 3 platform-services | Platform services | Identity tokens, entitlements & commerce, privileges, social graph, achievements, leaderboards, cloud save, region/age policy. | req ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK'] \nC-LOC 3 localization-i18n | Localized strings | String IDs, formatting, locale switching. | req ['C-ASSET'] \nC-UI 3 ui-architect | UI widgets & binding | Widget model, data binding, focus, layout. | req ['C-REFL', 'C-INPUT', 'C-DRAW2D', 'C-TEXT', 'C-LOC'] \nC-NAV 3 navigation-pathfinding | Navigation queries | Path requests, navmesh/grid queries, dynamic obstacles. | req ['C-SPATIAL'] \nC-GAME 4 gameplay-architect | Gameplay framework extension | Game module entry points, rules/session state, data-oriented control binding (input source or AI → controlled entity), scheduled gameplay systems, extension hooks. | req ['C-ID', 'C-FRAME'] \nC-SCRIPT 3 scripting-runtime | Script bindings | Binding generation, sandbox limits, script lifecycle. | req ['C-REFL'] \nC-SAVE 3 persistence-save | Save games | Save participation, versioned save records, async save/load. | req ['C-SER', 'C-ID'] \nC-COOK 5 content-pipeline-architect | Cook-step processors | Processor inputs, cache keys, determinism class (bit-exact / tolerance / pinned-artifact), platform variants, world-scope steps, per-asset on-demand invocation, validation hooks. | req ['C-ASSET', 'C-SER', 'C-TASK'] \nC-EDCMD 5 editor-architect | Editor commands & tool extension | Transactions, undo/redo, selection, tool registration. | req ['C-REFL', 'C-SER'] \nC-GRAPH 5 graph-editor-framework | Graph authoring & compilation | Node/pin model, validation, compilation hooks for domain graphs. | req ['C-EDCMD'] \nC-BUILD 5 build-system-toolchains | Build description | Targets, configurations, toolchains, codegen steps. | req [] \nC-PKG 5 packaging-release-patching | Release packages & patches | Package manifests, patch/DLC chunks, version compatibility. | req ['C-VFS', 'C-BUILD'] \nC-ARCH P engine-architect | Architecture, layering & profiles | Layer rules, contract registry, configuration profiles, conventions. | req [] \nC-ADR P architecture-governance | ADR & fitness functions | ADR template incl. revisit conditions; automated architectural checks. | req [] \nC-EVID P research-evidence | Evidence grading | Source tiers, maturity classes, claim standards. | req [] \nC-ORCH P program-orchestration | Agent coordination protocol | Ownership ledger with access classes; write sets by module convention (src/<skill-id>/, tools/<skill-id>/; tests owned by the test-owning skill); shared-file protocol; contributor semantics (review + change request, neve | req [] \nC-TEST P test-architect | Test & validation definition of done | Required test kinds per skill, test determinism, coverage & mutation thresholds, the evidence bundle an implementer hands to S3/S4 critics, oracle independence, conformance suites owned by contract owners with consumer-d | req [] \nC-API P api-lifecycle-migration | API stability & deprecation | Public vs internal APIs, versioning, deprecation windows, upgraders. | req [] \nC-TRUST P security-engineering | Trust boundaries | Untrusted inputs list, validation obligations, sandbox rules. | req [] \nC-A11Y P accessibility | Accessibility requirements | Mapped guideline requirements per player-facing feature. | req [] \nC-BASE 0 platform-architect | Bootstrap base | Raw page allocator, raw log/assert/abort sink, monotonic clock, raw thread primitives and late-bound hook tables that higher layers install (allocator, log sink, assert handler, crash annotator). Depends on nothing. | req [] \nC-LIFETIME 1 core-runtime-architect | Ownership & retirement | Engine-wide ownership and cross-thread reference rules; deferred-destruction/retirement service keyed to completion tokens (task completion, frames in flight, GPU fences). | req ['C-SYNC'] \nC-IPC 2 core-runtime-architect | Engine IPC | Process model and IPC/RPC transport for editor↔runtime, tool workers, crash handler, profiler and script debugger; dev-only port security. | req ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK'] \nC-SCALE 1 runtime-scalability | Scalability & governor | Device-profile knobs, scalability cvars, budget query/report API, actuator registration and governor control signals. | req ['C-CFG'] \nC-FLOW 2 frame-orchestration | Cross-subsystem data channels | Versioned snapshots, double/triple-buffered hand-off, mailboxes and multi-rate resampling between subsystems; producer/consumer declared per channel. The default for runtime data flow; global barriers need an ADR. | req ['C-FRAME'] \nC-PRESENT 2 frame-orchestration | Present timeline | Present timeline and display-time prediction, latency markers, interposed presenters (frame generation, XR compositor, cloud encoder), GPU-frame-complete and present-feedback sink implemented by the RHI (dependency inver | req ['C-FRAME'] \nC-SNAPSHOT 2 determinism-replay | Frame-state snapshot & resimulation | Snapshot/restore, resimulate N ticks, history ring, per-participant cost declaration. | req ['C-FRAME', 'C-SER'] \nC-REPLAY 3 determinism-replay | Replay container & streams | Replay container, timeline, stream registration (input, replication, visual log, animation debug, external/nondeterministic inputs) and cross-build versioning. | req ['C-SNAPSHOT', 'C-SER'] \nC-VIEW 2 spatial-transforms | Views & view arbitration | View registry: view sources (gameplay camera, cinematic, editor, photo mode, XR pose) with priority/blend stack and shake/FOV channels, per-local-player views, view origin for LWC rebasing; derived listener and streaming | req ['C-SPATIAL'] \nC-SIGNIF 2 world-architect | Significance & simulation tiers | Per-entity significance, simulation tier and update budget, computed once from views/players (all players on a server) and consumed by each domain's LOD policy. | req ['C-VIEW'] \nC-ENV 3 world-architect | Environment queries | Environment query service: ground height/surface type, water surface/volume (height, velocity, depth, body id), wind field, weather parameters, deformation deltas; implemented by terrain, water, atmosphere and voxel prov | req ['C-SPATIAL'] \nC-GPUTIER 2 gpu-platform-architect | GPU feature tiers | Named GPU feature tiers (binding model, pipeline-state model, queue topology, mesh/RT/tensor support, memory model) and the API baseline each tier maps to; render features declare the minimum tier they need. | req ['C-RHI'] \nC-INSTANCES 3 geometry-pipeline | Instance scene | Persistent instance/primitive handles, batched add/remove/update with delta upload (cost O(changes)), instance data layout shared with the ray-tracing instance builder; served by both CPU and GPU submission paths. | req ['C-RG', 'C-GPUMEM'] \nC-GEOLOD 3 virtualized-geometry-lod | Geometry LOD & page residency | Cluster/LOD selection and page residency for raster, shadow and ray-tracing consumers. | req ['C-RG'] \nC-VT 3 texture-streaming-vt | Texture residency & virtual texturing | Texture residency requests, VT page tables/feedback and allocation for terrain, materials and runtime-composited textures. | req ['C-RG', 'C-GPUMEM'] \nC-LIGHT 3 direct-lighting-shadows | Direct lighting sampling | Light lists (clustered or stochastic), shadow lookups, light units, many-light sampling API for any shading point incl. translucency, volumes and particles. | req ['C-RSCENE'] \nC-GI 3 global-illumination | Indirect lighting sampling | Indirect diffuse/specular sampling for any shading point (incl. translucent and volumetric), probes, sky/environment lighting. | req ['C-RSCENE'] \nC-ATMOS 3 atmosphere-weather | Atmosphere & participating media | Aerial perspective, froxel/local media volumes, cloud shadows, weather-driven global material parameters. | req ['C-RSCENE'] \nC-VIDEO 3 media-playback | Video surfaces | Video playback sessions, surfaces as textures, timing against the audio clock. | req ['C-RG'] \nC-DEVICE 2 input-devices-haptics | Input devices & haptics | Device enumeration, raw state and events with timestamps, device↔platform-user pairing, haptic, trigger-effect and LED output, virtual device injection for automation. | req ['C-PAL'] \nC-NETLINK 2 network-transport | Network links & sessions | Sessions, channels, reliability/ordering classes, send budgets, link statistics, connection events; used by replication, voice, rollback input exchange and telemetry streams. | req ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK'] \nC-REP 3 replication | Replication | Replicated state declaration, relevancy hooks, RPCs, net IDs, batch registration, replay and spectator streams. | req ['C-NETLINK', 'C-SER', 'C-ID'] \nC-PREDICT 3 prediction-rollback | Prediction & rollback | Predicted/rollback-able state registration, tick-stamped input history, resimulation hooks, rewind queries, cosmetic-effect suppression during resim. | req ['C-REP', 'C-DET', 'C-SNAPSHOT', 'C-INPUT'] \nC-MOVE 4 character-movement | Character movement | Movement modes, move requests, resimulatable move API, root-motion hand-off. 