{"parentUuid":"af875e38-079d-49c4-9560-42c56ced139d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a7253f978e1829a88","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H6xsuYq71d4EXcBBiuDcP6","type":"tool_result","content":"   PLAT.SVC.moderation | Moderation boundary (UGC, chat, generated content) | online-services-liveops | E |modding-ugc \n   PLAT.SVC.emulation | Service test doubles & outage injection | online-services-liveops | E |robustness-fuzzing \n   CORE.LIFE.services | Service registry & dependency-injection policy (no hidden globals) | core-runtime-architect | E  \n   CORE.FRAME.test-clock | Injectable/controllable clocks for tests | frame-orchestration | E  \n   WLD.PCG.ml | ML-generated content | procedural-generation | X  \n   RND.RHI.gpu-work | GPU-generated work primitives (indirect, device-generated commands, work-graph programs, backing memory) | rhi-core | E |render-graph-scheduling,geometry-pipeline \n   RND.GRAPH.work-graphs | Scheduling, barriers & memory for GPU-generated work incl. work graphs | render-graph-scheduling | E  \n   RND.SHADER.binding-abstraction | Shader-side binding abstraction generated per binding tier | shader-system | E |rhi-core \n   INP.DEV.injection | Virtual input device injection for bots & tests | input-devices-haptics | E |functional-automation-soak \n   GAM.AI.llm | LLM-driven NPC dialogue & behavior (via C-AIAGENT; guardrails per XC.SEC.genai) | ai-behavior-perception | M  \n   ED.AI.provenance | Provenance of generated content (consumer of CNT.ID.rights) | ai-assisted-authoring | M |certification-compliance,content-pipeline-architect \n   QA.ROBUST.faults | Fault injection (IO errors, OOM, device lost) | robustness-fuzzing | E  \n   QA.CERT.genai | Rating & platform disclosure for runtime-generated content | certification-compliance | E |ai-behavior-perception \n   OBS.CRASH.privacy | Client-side redaction of secrets/PII in dumps & logs, annotation allow-lists, retention | crash-diagnostics | E |security-engineering,observability-telemetry \n # XC.SEC Security {}\n   XC.SEC.threats | Threat modeling | security-engineering | E  \n   XC.SEC.coding | Secure coding & memory-safety policy | security-engineering | E  \n   XC.SEC.trust | Trust boundaries for untrusted input | security-engineering | E  \n   XC.SEC.supply-chain | Supply-chain security (SBOM, signing, reproducible builds) | security-engineering | E |build-system-toolchains \n   XC.SEC.secrets | Secrets management | security-engineering | E |ci-cd-automation \n   XC.SEC.tamper | Anti-tamper & DRM boundary | security-engineering | E |anti-cheat-integrity \n   XC.SEC.privacy | Privacy engineering | security-engineering | E  \n   XC.SEC.sandbox | Mod / UGC sandbox policy | security-engineering | E |modding-ugc \n   XC.SEC.server-validation | Server-side cheat validation | anti-cheat-integrity | E | |[[\"online\"]]\n   XC.SEC.anticheat | Client anti-cheat middleware integration boundary | anti-cheat-integrity | E | |[[\"online\"]]\n   XC.SEC.abuse | Exploit & economy-abuse detection signals | anti-cheat-integrity | E |platform-services |[[\"online\"]]\n   XC.SEC.score-integrity | Leaderboard & achievement submission validation | anti-cheat-integrity | E  \n   XC.SEC.memory-safety | Memory-safety posture: hardened library modes, shipping bounds checks, memory-safe language for untrusted-input parsers, MTE/PAC | security-engineering | M |core-runtime-architect \n   XC.SEC.hardening | Exploit-mitigation & hardened-build matrix per platform (CFI, shadow stacks, allocator hardening) | security-engineering | E |build-system-toolchains,memory-allocators \n   XC.SEC.crypto-policy | Cryptography & TLS/certificate policy | security-engineering | E |containers-core-types \n   XC.SEC.vuln-response | Vulnerability intake, disclosure, severity SLAs & patch path to shipped titles | security-engineering | E |packaging-release-patching,api-lifecycle-migration,build-release-architect \n   XC.SEC.incident | Live incident-response runbooks for online titles | security-engineering | E |online-services-liveops,anti-cheat-integrity \n   XC.SEC.dev-trust | Project/workspace trust, plugin signing & permissions, sandboxed import of untrusted source assets | security-engineering | E |plugin-system,editor-architect,asset-import-interchange \n   XC.SEC.agent-boundary | Development-agent capability scoping, sandboxing, egress & prompt-injection threat model | security-engineering | E |program-orchestration,ci-cd-automation \n   XC.SEC.genai | Generative-feature threat model: prompt injection, output handling, PII, cost DoS | security-engineering | M |ai-behavior-perception,ai-assisted-authoring,online-services-liveops \n   XC.SEC.data-rights | Data inventory, retention & data-subject request flow | security-engineering | E |certification-compliance,observability-telemetry,crash-diagnostics \n   XC.SEC.testing | Pen testing, red-teaming, secret scanning & shipping-build hardening audit | security-engineering | E |robustness-fuzzing,ci-cd-automation,visual-debugging-tools \n===== program-orchestration ['all'] process [] None\nTurns architecture into coordinated multi-agent work: decomposes milestones into tasks by skill territory, keeps the ownership ledger and territory locks, sequences integration through vertical slices, routes contract change requests, and schedules critic gates.\n[['Deciding architecture', 'engine-architect'], ['CI mechanics', 'ci-cd-automation'], ['Release versioning', 'build-release-architect']]\n['C-PROD']\n===== test-architect ['all'] process [] None\nTest strategy and architecture: per-subsystem test pyramid, frameworks, the test definition of done every skill must meet, contract tests, test content, coverage and mutation policy, flakiness policy.\n[['Running pipelines', 'ci-cd-automation'], ['Performance regression', 'perf-benchmarking'], ['Rendering image validation', 'render-validation']]\n[]\n===== functional-automation-soak ['all'] process [] None\nGame-level automation: scripted and bot playthroughs, smoke/boot tests, soak and stability runs (memory growth, leaks), hardware/OS compatibility matrix, network harnesses and server load tests.\n[['Unit test frameworks', 'test-architect'], ['Device-farm infrastructure', 'ci-cd-automation']]\n['C-GAME?', 'C-INPUT?', 'C-NET?']\n===== security-engineering ['all'] process [] None\nThreat modeling and trust boundaries for every untrusted input, secure-coding and memory-safety policy, supply-chain security, secrets, anti-tamper boundary, privacy engineering, mod/UGC sandbox policy.\n[['Cheat detection', 'anti-cheat-integrity'], ['Fuzzing campaigns', 'robustness-fuzzing'], ['Transport encryption implementation', 'network-transport']]\n[]\n===== modding-ugc ['ugc'] runtime ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] None\nMod and UGC support: mod SDK, content overrides via VFS layering, sandboxed mod scripting, UGC upload and moderation boundaries, mod compatibility across patches.\n[['Sandbox policy', 'security-engineering'], ['Script VM', 'scripting-runtime']]\n['C-VFS', 'C-SCRIPT', 'C-PLUGIN', 'C-SVC']\n===== procedural-generation ['openworld'] runtime ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] None\nDeterministic graph-based PCG framework usable in editor and at stream-in, placement and scattering rules, grammar and constraint methods; evaluates ML generation.\n[['Foliage-specific rules', 'vegetation-foliage'], ['Graph editor UI', 'graph-editor-framework']]\n['C-WORLD', 'C-DET', 'C-ML?', 'C-INSTANCES?']\n===== visual-debugging-tools ['all'] runtime ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] None\nDebug draw API, in-game console and cheats, runtime entity inspector and gameplay debugger, visual logger and rewind, debug menus and overlays.\n[['Logging and traces', 'observability-telemetry'], ['Render buffer visualization', 'render-architect']]\n['C-INSTR', 'C-ECS?', 'C-DRAW2D?', 'C-RSCENE?', 'C-REPLAY?', 'C-IPC']\n===== rhi-webgpu ['all'] runtime ['client', 'tools'] ['web']\nImplements C-RHI on WebGPU (bind groups, implicit sync, limits tiers); owns its validation-layer runs and vendor/driver quirks.\n[['RHI abstraction & capability model', 'rhi-core'], ['Other API backends', 'rhi-core']]\n['C-PAL', 'C-SYNC', 'C-GPUTIER']","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8b8139f0-90f7-49b1-835a-4af2203e41ab","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:23:24.299Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"af875e38-079d-49c4-9560-42c56ced139d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
