e8abddcd4","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:23:44.359Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
{"parentUuid":"61feabd7-738b-4e54-bbd8-33de8abddcd4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a7253f978e1829a88","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018i2E18U4rHPccvUdTLKDKD","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/06-gap-analysis.md:5:- **Thin evidence.** Where authoritative information is scarce, so an agent cannot \"look up the answer\".\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:21:| A6 | Work graphs in production | The spec is shipped and vendor samples exist, but there are almost no shipped-title postmortems. Performance varies by vendor and driver. | render-graph-scheduling | Benchmark work-graph vs indirect-dispatch implementations of one GPU-dri\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:22:| A7 | Neural rendering in shipped games (neural texture compression, neural materials, neural radiance caching) | Research and SDK demos exist; production evidence is limited and depends on tensor/cooperative-vector support. | texture-streaming-vt, material-system, ml-inf\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:23:| A8 | Learned animation in production (learned motion matching, neural controllers) | Strong research (SIGGRAPH), few production postmortems; memory/runtime vs quality trade-offs are title-specific. | motion-synthesis | Keep classic motion matching as the baseline. A lear\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:26:| A11 | Memory-safety posture for a C++ engine | Guidance exists (hardening modes, safe subsets, Rust interop), but there is little production evidence for engines specifically. | security-engineering, core-runtime-architect | ADR: which layers must accept untrusted input,\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:27:| A12 | LLM-driven NPCs | Latency, cost, safety/moderation, determinism and age-rating implications are largely unresolved. Evidence is mostly demos. | ai-behavior-perception | `experimental`. It is only allowed behind an optional contract with moderation (platform-service\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:30:| A13 | Validation of autonomous-agent-produced engine code | New discipline; little evidence on failure modes of agent-written systems code at this scale. | test-architect, program-orchestration | Mutation testing to detect vacuous tests; independent critic gates per stag\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:46:| B9 | Shading language | HLSL (DXC) vs Slang vs cross-compiled | shader-system | Multi-backend reach (SPIR-V, Metal, DXIL), modules/generics, tooling maturity, Khronos governance of Slang. |\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:59:| B22 | Binding model per tier | Bindless vs descriptor buffers vs bounded bind groups | gpu-platform-architect, rhi-core | Backend and device limits (WebGPU, Android descriptor indexing). |\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:62:| B25 | Gameplay control model | Possession-style controller/pawn vs data-oriented control binding vs genre-specific | gameplay-architect | Genre, multiplayer model, input-to-entity cardinality. |\ndocs/07-research-plan.md:8:- **Platform holders and vendors:** Microsoft DirectX specs and DirectX Developer Blog (spec announcements count as T2), Xbox/PlayStation/Nintendo developer documentation (licensed), Khronos (Vulkan spec, registry and profiles; SPIR-V; glTF; KTX; OpenXR; Slang), Apple Meta\ndocs/07-research-plan.md:10:- **Studio technical publications:** EA SEED / Frostbite, Ubisoft (Snowdrop, Anvil), Activision Central Tech research publications, id Software talks, Guerrilla (Decima) publications, Remedy (Northlight), Capcom (RE Engine CEDEC talks), Naughty Dog, Insomniac, Epic, Unity\ndocs/07-research-plan.md:19:| **Platform** | platform-architect and platform experts | Licensed console documentation; Windows GameInput, GDK and DirectStorage docs; Android Game Development Kit (AGDK), Android performance tuner; Apple game porting and Metal docs; Steam Deck compatibility guidance; \ndocs/07-research-plan.md:23:| **Rendering architecture** | render-architect, rhi-core, render-graph-scheduling, gpu-memory-resources | FrameGraph (O'Donnell, GDC 2017); D3D12 Enhanced Barriers spec; D3D12 Work Graphs spec and AMD/NVIDIA work-graph samples; Vulkan synchronization2, descriptor buffers\ndocs/07-research-plan.md:25:| **Lighting, shadows, GI, RT, PT** | direct-lighting-shadows, global-illumination, ray-tracing-infrastructure, path-tracing | ReSTIR (Bitterli et al., SIGGRAPH 2020); ReSTIR GI (Ouyang et al., HPG 2021); GRIS / ReSTIR PT (Lin et al., SIGGRAPH 2022); \"A Gentle Introductio\ndocs/07-research-plan.md:28:| **Textures & neural compression** | texture-streaming-vt, ml-inference-runtime | Sampler feedback spec (D3D12); virtual texturing talks (id Tech MegaTexture history as foundational; modern SVT/RVT docs); \"Random-Access Neural Compression of Material Textures\" (Vaidyanat\ndocs/07-research-plan.md:29:| **Novel scene representations** | render-architect (radar), research-evidence | 3D Gaussian Splatting (Kerbl et al., SIGGRAPH 2023) and follow-ups on real-time rasterization and streaming — `experimental` for games. |\ndocs/07-research-plan.md:42:| **ML runtime** | ml-inference-runtime | DirectML and cooperative-vector specs; ONNX spec; vendor neural-shading SDKs; quantization literature. |\ndocs/07-research-plan.md:47:2. **Grade.** Grade each source (T1–T6) and give each technique a maturity class.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f216fd4e-0ed6-448b-a7ba-d6e16bb5e21d","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:23:44.421Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"61feabd7-738b-4e54-bbd8-33de8abddcd4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
